- WHAT DOES IT MEAN?
- SASHAY.

240
00:09:42,518 --> 00:09:43,519
YOU SASHAY.

241
00:09:43,519 --> 00:09:46,623
YOU WERE IN PARIS FOR...

242
00:09:46,623 --> 00:09:48,324
WITH THE TWIRL AND THE PURSE

243
00:09:48,324 --> 00:09:49,626
AND THE--OH, YEAH.

244
00:09:49,626 --> 00:09:52,028
SASHAY, CHANTE.

245
00:09:52,028 --> 00:09:53,563
I DON'T EVEN HAVE MY WALK DOWN.

246
00:09:53,563 --> 00:09:55,999
I DEFINITELY DON'T HAVE
MY SIGNATURE WALK DOWN.

247
00:09:55,999 --> 00:09:57,934
LIKE, I DON'T KNOW
WHAT I'M GONNA DO.

248
00:09:57,934 --> 00:10:01,471
THEN WE DO A SWIRL, END.

249
00:10:01,471 --> 00:10:02,572
LIKE, I DON'T FEEL LIKE
I'M STICKING MY BUTT OUT,

250
00:10:02,572 --> 00:10:03,973
BUT I GUESS IT'S OUT.

251
00:10:03,973 --> 00:10:05,241
LESLIE'S NOT A GOOD WALKER,

252
00:10:05,241 --> 00:10:06,242
FLAT OUT.

253
00:10:06,242 --> 00:10:07,577
SHE WAS THE DUCK BOOTY.

254
00:10:07,577 --> 00:10:09,245
THAT'S THE GIRL WITH
THE DUCK BOOTY WALK.

255
00:10:09,245 --> 00:10:10,680
I THINK YOU JUST HAVE
A LONGER BUTT.

256
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:11,948
I HAVE A SMALL, LITTLE BUTT.

257
00:10:11,948 --> 00:10:13,082
I DON'T KNOW, I NEED TO WATCH,

258
00:10:13,082 --> 00:10:14,317
LIKE, RUNWAY MORE, BECAUSE,

259
00:10:14,317 --> 00:10:16,486
I STILL FEEL LIKE I JUST
DON'T KNOW WHAT I'M DOING.

260
00:10:16,486 --> 00:10:17,620
I FEEL LIKE I'VE BEEN HEARING

261
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:20,123
A LOT OF THE SAME STUFF
ABOUT OWNING MY HEIGHT,

262
00:10:20,123 --> 00:10:21,457
BUT IT'S HARD,
BECAUSE I DON'T REALLY KNOW

263
00:10:21,457 --> 00:10:23,927
HOW TO PRACTICE THAT.

264
00:10:23,927 --> 00:10:25,495
OH, THAT WAS CAKE...

265
00:10:25,495 --> 00:10:26,696
HUH?

266
00:10:26,696 --> 00:10:28,464
- THE WAY IT JUST CAME OFF.
- YEAH.

267
00:10:28,464 --> 00:10:30,633
IT'S WEIRD, IT'S LIKE THERE'S A
BUNCH OF OTHER GIRLS HERE,

268
00:10:30,633 --> 00:10:32,135
BUT I FEEL REALLY LONELY.

269
00:10:32,135 --> 00:10:33,269
THAT FUNNY?

270
00:10:33,269 --> 00:10:34,370
Sorry, baby.

271
00:10:34,370 --> 00:10:35,571
So what'd you guys do today?

272
00:10:35,571 --> 00:10:37,407
WE'RE DOING
RUNWAY STUFF AGAIN

273
00:10:37,407 --> 00:10:39,309
THAT'S, LIKE,
EVEN MORE COMPLICATED NOW.

274
00:10:39,309 --> 00:10:40,310
That's really decent stuff.

275
00:10:40,310 --> 00:10:41,577
You can really sell that.

276
00:10:41,577 --> 00:10:45,214
I FEEL LIKE I'VE BEEN
SLOUCHING SO MUCH MORE.

277
00:10:45,214 --> 00:10:46,950
I'M HERE WITH PEOPLE
WHO HAVE BEEN TRYING

278
00:10:46,950 --> 00:10:50,553
TO GET INTO MODELING FOR YEARS,
AND I WAS FOUND IN A MALL.

279
00:10:50,553 --> 00:10:52,255
THAT JUST MAKES ME WANNA
SHOW THEM THAT

280
00:10:52,255 --> 00:10:54,023
I REALLY WANNA BE HERE
AND THAT I DESERVE IT.

281
00:10:54,023 --> 00:10:55,525
Well, it's probably
gonna get more stressful.

282
00:10:55,525 --> 00:10:57,160
DEFINITELY,
I'M JUST--YEAH.

283
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:59,362
♪♪♪

284
00:11:03,333 --> 00:11:05,568
TYRA MAIL SAYS,
"SASHAY, CHANTE."

285
00:11:05,568 --> 00:11:07,036
I THOUGHT OF RuPAUL.

286
00:11:07,036 --> 00:11:08,037
WASN'T THAT, LIKE, HIS PHRASE?

287
00:11:08,037 --> 00:11:09,739
OKAY, WE'RE GONNA BE DOING DRAG?

288
00:11:09,739 --> 00:11:12,075
(Handel's "Messiah"
playing on organ)

289
00:11:15,445 --> 00:11:18,348
WHAT CAN WE POSSIBLY
BE DOING IN A CHURCH?

290
00:11:18,348 --> 00:11:20,249
BUT, OF COURSE, I BLESSED MYSELF
WITH THE HOLY WATER--

291
00:11:20,249 --> 00:11:23,353
DIP, DIP, DIP, DIP, DIP.

292
00:11:23,353 --> 00:11:25,588
DAD'S A PREACHER--
RAISED IN THE CHURCH.

293
00:11:25,588 --> 00:11:27,623
WHEN I WAS IN THE WOMB,
I'VE NEVER MISSED A SUNDAY,

294
00:11:27,623 --> 00:11:28,424
LET'S JUST PUT IT THAT WAY.

295
00:11:28,424 --> 00:11:29,926
HELLO, LADIES.

296
00:11:29,926 --> 00:11:31,995
MY NAME IS ROY CAMPBELL,
AND I'M A PRODUCER

297
00:11:31,995 --> 00:11:33,496
OF SPECIAL EVENTS
AND FASHION SHOWS.

298
00:11:33,496 --> 00:11:35,698
I ALSO HAVE DONE EVENTS
FOR TYRA BANKS

299
00:11:35,698 --> 00:11:37,000
WHO'S A GOOD FRIEND OF MINE.

300
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,302
I FIRST MET TYRA
AFTER SHE DEBUTED IN PARIS

301
00:11:39,302 --> 00:11:40,603
DURING HER FIRST SEASON.

302
00:11:40,603 --> 00:11:43,339
NOW IF YOU'RE WONDERING
WHY YOU'RE HERE IN THE CHURCH,

303
00:11:43,339 --> 00:11:45,141
YESTERDAY, MISS J.
TAUGHT YOU

304
00:11:45,141 --> 00:11:47,143
HOW TO REMOVE GARMENTS
ON THE RUNWAY,

305
00:11:47,143 --> 00:11:50,179
AND THE TWINS SHOWED YOU
HOW TO SWIRL AND TWIRL.

306
00:11:50,179 --> 00:11:51,414
TODAY YOU'RE GONNA BE TESTED

307
00:11:51,414 --> 00:11:53,616
- IN A CHURCH FASHION SHOW.
- ♪ HALLELUJAH ♪

308
00:11:53,616 --> 00:11:55,218
OKAY.

309
00:11:55,218 --> 00:11:56,619
- ♪ HALLELUJAH ♪
- ANYTHING THAT HAS TO DO

310
00:11:56,619 --> 00:11:59,389
WITH RUNWAY, I DON'T CARE
IF IT'S IN THE SAHARA DESERT.

311
00:11:59,389 --> 00:12:02,258
IF THERE'S A RUNWAY,
JADE IS GONNA BE ON IT.

312
00:12:02,258 --> 00:12:04,227
IN THE EARLY '40s,
BLACKS COULD NOT

313
00:12:04,227 --> 00:12:05,395
GO TO FASHION SHOWS.

314
00:12:05,395 --> 00:12:07,330
THEY HAD TO PRESENT
THEIR OWN FASHION SHOWS.

315
00:12:07,330 --> 00:12:09,232
CHURCH FASHION SHOWS
ARE A BIG TRADITION

316
00:12:09,232 --> 00:12:10,400
IN THE BLACK COMMUNITY.

317
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:14,037
FOR TODAY'S TEST,
WE EXPECT YOU TO SASHAY, SWIRL,

318
00:12:14,037 --> 00:12:17,206
TWIRL, AND MAKE THOSE CLOTHES
COME ALIVE,

319
00:12:17,206 --> 00:12:18,608
AND WE INVITED
THE WHOLE CONGREGATION

320
00:12:18,608 --> 00:12:23,079
OF THIS CHURCH TO WATCH YOU
WORK THOSE GARMENTS.

321
00:12:23,079 --> 00:12:24,347
I WAS NERVOUS.

322
00:12:24,347 --> 00:12:27,116
I HAVE SO MUCH TROUBLE ALREADY
WALKING NORMALLY.

323
00:12:27,116 --> 00:12:29,485
HOW AM I SUPPOSED TO SWIRL
AND BE DRAMATIC?

324
00:12:29,485 --> 00:12:31,120
AND TODAY'S JUDGES
ARE TWO DESIGNERS

325
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,121
YOU'LL BE WORKING WITH--

326
00:12:32,121 --> 00:12:34,490
WORLD-RENOWNED DESIGNER
LLOYD KLEIN.

327
00:12:34,490 --> 00:12:36,192
- HELLO, LLOYD, WELCOME.
- HELLO, HOW ARE YOU?

328
00:12:36,192 --> 00:12:37,627
- I'M GOOD.
- HELLO, HELLO, HELLO.

329
00:12:37,627 --> 00:12:39,262
I'M SO HAPPY TO MEET YOU.

330
00:12:39,262 --> 00:12:42,498
AND WE HAVE
DIAMOND DESIGNER SOL RAFAEL.

331
00:12:42,498 --> 00:12:43,666
(applause)

332
00:12:43,666 --> 00:12:45,368
HI, LADIES.

333
00:12:45,368 --> 00:12:47,637
LLOYD AND I, WE GONNA CHOOSE
ONE WINNER WHO WE FEEL

334
00:12:47,637 --> 00:12:50,039
HAS THE BEST BODY MOVEMENT
ON THE RUNWAY,

335
00:12:50,039 --> 00:12:52,608
AND THAT GIRL IS GONNA BE
GETTING A HUGE PRIZE OF

336
00:12:52,608 --> 00:12:55,278
$25,000 DIAMOND RING.

337
00:12:55,278 --> 00:12:56,446
WOW.

338
00:12:56,446 --> 00:12:58,314
SHOW THOSE CLOTHES OFF
AND WIN THAT PRIZE.

339
00:12:58,314 --> 00:12:59,649
DANG.

340
00:12:59,649 --> 00:13:02,151
EVERYBODY IS SO CRYING,
THEY'RE LIKE, "DIAMONDS?

341
00:13:02,151 --> 00:13:03,152
DIAMONDS?"

342
00:13:03,152 --> 00:13:04,487
♪♪♪

343
00:13:04,487 --> 00:13:05,555
OKAY, EVERYONE.

344
00:13:05,555 --> 00:13:07,190
FIRST LOOK NOW.

345
00:13:07,190 --> 00:13:08,524
THE SHOW IS GONNA START.

346
00:13:08,524 --> 00:13:09,926
I LOVE THIS COLOR.

347
00:13:09,926 --> 00:13:11,194
I WAS SCARED
BEFORE I CAME HERE,

348
00:13:11,194 --> 00:13:13,296
JUST BECAUSE
I NEVER WEAR HIGH HEELS.

349
00:13:13,296 --> 00:13:14,564
LIKE, I WAS SCARED
OF HIGH HEELS

350
00:13:14,564 --> 00:13:17,100
BECAUSE I'M JUST LIKE,
I'M GONNA FALL ON MY BUTT.

351
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:19,035
GORGEOUS DRESSES,
BUT I DON'T KNOW IF I COULD

352
00:13:19,035 --> 00:13:20,336
REALLY ASWIRL AROUND

353
00:13:20,336 --> 00:13:22,004
AND REALLY SHOW OFF
A LOT OF FABRIC.

354
00:13:22,004 --> 00:13:25,108
♪♪♪

355
00:13:25,108 --> 00:13:27,176
GET READY
TO SHOUT "HALLELUJAH"

356
00:13:27,176 --> 00:13:29,645
AND TO SCREAM "AMEN."
(cheering)

357
00:13:32,448 --> 00:13:36,486
TALK ABOUT MAKING
A DRAMATIC ENTRANCE...

358
00:13:36,486 --> 00:13:38,688
DANIELLE
NEEDS MORE PERSONALITY

359
00:13:38,688 --> 00:13:40,523
ON THE RUNWAY, DEFINITELY.

360
00:13:40,523 --> 00:13:43,459
BUT AS MY MAMA USED TO SAY,
"YOU AIN'T SEEN NOTHIN' YET."

361
00:13:43,459 --> 00:13:46,062
(cheering)

362
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,302
YOU WALK OUT THERE,
AND THE ENERGY WAS JUST GREAT.

363
00:13:53,302 --> 00:13:55,138
WORK IT, WORK IT.

364
00:13:55,138 --> 00:13:57,240
I PULLED OUT OF MY MIND,
"NOW WALK STRAIGHT."

365
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:58,307
I WAS LIKE,
"I'M WORKIN' MY HIPS,

366
00:13:58,307 --> 00:14:01,310
AND IF MISS J.
DOESN'T LIKE THAT, TOO BAD."

367
00:14:01,310 --> 00:14:02,612
THE DRESSES I WAS WEARING
WAS VERY DIFFICULT

368
00:14:02,612 --> 00:14:04,413
FOR MYSELF TO WALK IN.

369
00:14:04,413 --> 00:14:07,350
SO I WAS REALLY WORRIED THAT
I WAS GONNA END UP TRIPPING.

370
00:14:07,350 --> 00:14:08,351
DON'T BE SHY.

371
00:14:08,351 --> 00:14:10,386
YOU'RE ON THE CATWALK NOW.

372
00:14:10,386 --> 00:14:13,022
THAT'S IT, SWIRL AND TWIRL.

373
00:14:13,022 --> 00:14:16,125
BROOKE NEEDS TO WORK
ON HER PRESENCE.

374
00:14:16,125 --> 00:14:17,994
SHE'S A LITTLE BIT ABSENT.

375
00:14:17,994 --> 00:14:22,098
OH, SASHAY DOWN THE RUNWAY.

376
00:14:22,098 --> 00:14:25,168
COME ON, THAT'S IT,
PUT SOME PEP IN YOUR STEP.

377
00:14:25,168 --> 00:14:27,003
I LIKE IT A LOT.
(laughs)

378
00:14:27,003 --> 00:14:28,604
THAT RUNWAY IS SUPER GREAT.

379
00:14:28,604 --> 00:14:30,139
MY ENERGY LEVEL WAS UP.

380
00:14:30,139 --> 00:14:32,008
JADE AND I CAN
REALLY COMPETE NOW,

381
00:14:32,008 --> 00:14:34,210
BECAUSE THAT'S ULTIMATELY
WHO I THINK IT'S BETWEEN.

382
00:14:34,210 --> 00:14:36,212
(shouting)

383
00:14:36,212 --> 00:14:38,414
SOMEBODY SAY "HALLELUJAH."

384
00:14:38,414 --> 00:14:39,649
(shouting)

385
00:14:39,649 --> 00:14:41,484
YOU GOT TO BREAK IT ON DOWN!

386
00:14:41,484 --> 00:14:42,485
YOU GOT TO GIVE IT UP.

387
00:14:42,485 --> 00:14:45,054
(cheering)

388
00:14:48,424 --> 00:14:50,626
SWIRL AND TWIRL.

389
00:14:50,626 --> 00:14:52,161
BREAK IT ON DOWN.

390
00:14:52,161 --> 00:14:53,429
- THAT A GIRL.
- I WOULD TAKE TWO STEPS

391
00:14:53,429 --> 00:14:57,366
AND I WOULD STEP ON THE TRAIN.

392
00:14:57,366 --> 00:14:59,335
I DIDN'T FEEL COMFORTABLE IN IT,
AND I'M SURE THAT SHOWED.

393
00:14:59,335 --> 00:15:00,336
YEAH!

394
00:15:00,336 --> 00:15:01,470
WHOO!

395
00:15:01,470 --> 00:15:02,638
WHOO!

396
00:15:02,638 --> 00:15:05,208
♪♪♪

397
00:15:08,644 --> 00:15:10,546
THAT'S RIGHT, AMEN TO THAT.

398
00:15:10,546 --> 00:15:12,415
THAT IS WONDERFUL!

399
00:15:12,415 --> 00:15:14,083
ONE OF THE DRESSERS SAID
I HAD ONE

400
00:15:14,083 --> 00:15:15,551
OF THE HOTTEST LOOKS TODAY,

401
00:15:15,551 --> 00:15:18,654
AND I'M DEFINITELY
GONNA WORK IT.

402
00:15:18,654 --> 00:15:19,589
I'M GONNA WORK IT OUT FOR GOD.

403
00:15:19,589 --> 00:15:23,426
♪♪♪

404
00:15:23,426 --> 00:15:26,462
I WAS TWIRLIN' MY BUTT OFF,
AND I'M THINKIN',

405
00:15:26,462 --> 00:15:27,697
"JADE, JUST PULL THIS OFF."

406
00:15:27,697 --> 00:15:32,368
TWIRL, TWIRL!

407
00:15:32,368 --> 00:15:35,204
JADE CAME OUT,
AND SHE JUST STARTED TURNING

408
00:15:35,204 --> 00:15:37,039
AND TWIRLING AND TWIRLING.

409
00:15:37,039 --> 00:15:40,443
THAT'S WHAT A COMMUNITY
FASHION SHOW IS ALL ABOUT.

410
00:15:40,443 --> 00:15:42,912
WE HAVE THE BEST ENERGY.

411
00:15:42,912 --> 00:15:45,181
I THINK I DID SHOW JADE UP.

412
00:15:45,181 --> 00:15:49,452
SO I THINK
I DEFINITELY WON THAT ONE.

413
00:15:49,452 --> 00:15:52,054
IT WAS VERY INTERESTING
TO SEE, UH, ALL OF YOU.

414
00:15:52,054 --> 00:15:56,659
I THINK SOL AND I
CHOSE A WINNER FOR THE BEST WAY

415
00:15:56,659 --> 00:15:59,395
YOU SHOWED THE CLOTHES
AND THE JEWELRY,

416
00:15:59,395 --> 00:16:01,530
AND THE WINNER...

417
00:16:01,530 --> 00:16:03,299
IS...

418
00:16:03,299 --> 00:16:04,300
JADE.

419
00:16:04,300 --> 00:16:05,968
OH, YES!

420
00:16:05,968 --> 00:16:07,036
WHOO!

421
00:16:07,036 --> 00:16:08,337
HEY, LOOK AT THIS GIRL!

422
00:16:08,337 --> 00:16:09,939
I WAS WORKING IT.

423
00:16:09,939 --> 00:16:11,140
I SHOULD HAVE WON.

424
00:16:11,140 --> 00:16:12,141
I'M SO MAD.

425
00:16:12,141 --> 00:16:13,643
AAH!

426
00:16:13,643 --> 00:16:15,144
JADE WAS TRIPPIN'.

427
00:16:15,144 --> 00:16:17,146
I MEAN, I FEEL HER, 'CAUSE
IT'S DIAMONDS YOU WINNIN',

428
00:16:17,146 --> 00:16:18,147
BUT CHILL OUT.

429
00:16:18,147 --> 00:16:21,484
YOU HAVE $25,000
DIAMOND RING.

430
00:16:21,484 --> 00:16:23,986
♪♪♪

431
00:16:23,986 --> 00:16:25,254
I GOT A LITTLE BONUS FOR YOU.

432
00:16:25,254 --> 00:16:26,589
I WANT YOU TO PICK
ONE OF YOUR FRIENDS,

433
00:16:26,589 --> 00:16:28,024
AND WE'RE GONNA GIVE HER

434
00:16:28,024 --> 00:16:30,293
A $10,000 DIAMOND RING
AS WELL.

435
00:16:30,293 --> 00:16:32,528
FURONDA.

436
00:16:32,528 --> 00:16:33,429
WE GOT ANOTHER BONUS FOR YOU.

437
00:16:33,429 --> 00:16:34,964
OKAY.

438
00:16:34,964 --> 00:16:36,599
WE WANT YOU TO PICK
ANOTHER FRIEND OF YOURS,

439
00:16:36,599 --> 00:16:40,369
AND WE'RE GONNA GIVE HER
$8,000 DIAMOND RING.

440
00:16:40,369 --> 00:16:41,270
NNENNA.

441
00:16:41,270 --> 00:16:43,239
(laughs)

442
00:16:43,239 --> 00:16:44,640
I NEVER EXPECTED
TO BE PICKED BY JADE.

443
00:16:44,640 --> 00:16:46,375
I'M NOT DISAPPOINTED
THAT I DIDN'T GET PICKED BY HER.

444
00:16:46,375 --> 00:16:48,344
I'M DISAPPOINTED
THAT I DIDN'T EARN IT MYSELF.

445
00:16:48,344 --> 00:16:50,012
THANK YOU.

446
00:16:50,012 --> 00:16:51,514
I WISH
I WOULD HAVE DONE BETTER.

447
00:16:51,514 --> 00:16:53,416
♪♪♪

448
00:16:53,416 --> 00:16:55,151
WHAT?

449
00:16:55,151 --> 00:16:58,454
YES, THANK YOU, JESUS.

450
00:16:58,454 --> 00:16:59,922
JADE HAS WON TWO CHALLENGES.

451
00:16:59,922 --> 00:17:00,923
FURONDA, YOU GOT ONE.

452
00:17:00,923 --> 00:17:02,158
I GOT ONE.

453
00:17:02,158 --> 00:17:03,092
- GOT ONE UNDER MY BELT.
- I HAVE ZERO.

454
00:17:03,092 --> 00:17:04,126
I'M SO COOL.

455
00:17:04,126 --> 00:17:07,630
HOW MANY HAVE YOU--
YOU--WHATEVER.

456
00:17:07,630 --> 00:17:08,731
YOU KNOW WHEN WE WERE
STANDIN' THERE WAITIN'

457
00:17:08,731 --> 00:17:10,366
FOR THE WINNER TO BE SAID?

458
00:17:10,366 --> 00:17:12,401
I WAS JUST LIKE,
"I DON'T WANT JADE TO WIN."

459
00:17:19,175 --> 00:17:20,675
I'M HERE TO DO WELL,

460
00:17:20,675 --> 00:17:23,112
NOT TO GET INVOLVED
IN THOSE LITTLE THINGS,

461
00:17:23,112 --> 00:17:25,314
BUT I DON'T LIKE NNENNA,
AND JUST BECAUSE

462
00:17:25,314 --> 00:17:27,650
I HANDLE MY STRESS
IN DIFFERENT WAYS THAN OTHERS

463
00:17:27,650 --> 00:17:29,418
DOESN'T MAKE ME A CRYBABY.

464
00:17:29,418 --> 00:17:32,954
♪♪♪

465
00:17:32,954 --> 00:17:33,955
HEY, DADDY.

466
00:17:33,955 --> 00:17:35,324
You okay?

467
00:17:35,324 --> 00:17:36,325
YEAH.

468
00:17:36,325 --> 00:17:37,426
(crying)

469
00:17:37,426 --> 00:17:39,662
I JUST HATE IT HERE SO MUCH.

470
00:17:39,662 --> 00:17:41,530
I don't wanna
hear you worrying too much.

471
00:17:41,530 --> 00:17:43,366
WELL, BECAUSE I SAID
SOMETHING I SHOULDN'T HAVE,

472
00:17:43,366 --> 00:17:46,369
'CAUSE, DAD, I CALLED HER
A NAME, AND I FEEL SO BAD.

473
00:17:46,369 --> 00:17:49,038
IT'S NOT REALLY LIKE ME
TO BE LIKE THAT.

474
00:17:49,038 --> 00:17:51,307
THERE'S JUST SO MUCH
OTHER PRESSURES

475
00:17:51,307 --> 00:17:54,510
TO, LIKE, DEAL WITH,
AND THEN THAT ADDED TO IT

